<sn><md>### South America

:::.row
:::.col-12 .col-lg-5

South America is the **fourth-largest continent** `4th` in the world. It is located primarily in the **Western Hemisphere** and mostly in the **Southern Hemisphere** `WS`.

It is famous for the **Amazon Rainforest**, the **Andes Mountains**, diverse cultures, and rich biodiversity.

There are **12 independent countries**:

| No. | Country   | Capital      |
| --- | --------- | ------------ |
| 1  | Suriname  | Paramaribo  (paradibo) |
| 2   | Guyana    | Georgetown  (george washington)  |
| 3  | Venezuela | Caracas   (circus)   |
| 4   | Colombia  | Bogotá   (money height)    |
| 5   | Ecuador   | Quito   (coto)     |
| 6   | Peru      | Lima         |
| 7   | Bolivia   | Sucre  (bolo viaya sorry)      |
| 8   | Paraguay  | Asunción  (ayshon)   |
| 9   | Chile     | Santiago     |
| 10   | Argentina | Buenos Aires (younus airplane) |
| 11  | Uruguay   | Montevideo   |
| 12   | Brazil    | Brasília     |


**French Guiana** is also located in South America, but it is an `overseas department of France` rather than an independent country.



